    ],
    "word_count": 52,
    "html": "<p>Georg Stratenwerth is a German investment professional and former partner at J.P. Morgan Partners and Advent International. He led private-equity operations in Germany and established Advent’s Mumbai office before returning to London. His later work included overseeing the Greek operations of Pillarstone, an investment platform created to restructure troubled bank loans.</p>\r\n"
  },
  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "At Be Caring, Georg Stratenwerth applied his financial experience to a social-care business facing heavy debts. As a non-executive director, he concentrated on finance and corporate governance. The company’s chairman singled out his support during its recovery, while crediting chief executive Sharon Lowrie and her team with the operational turnaround.\n\nStratenwerth also advises investment decisions at Big Issue Invest, which finances social enterprises. Through the Ashoka Support Network, he contributes financial and strategic support to social entrepreneurs. His environmental work includes serving as a trustee of ClientEarth, where legal expertise is used to protect nature and address environmental damage.",
    "confidence": {
      "score": 93,
      "band": "high",
      "reason": "Complete primary governance account distinguishes his board contribution from executive management and institutional lending."
    },
